<% content_for(:title, "find me by ear") %>
<main class="hunt" data-controller="hunt" data-hunt-url-value="<%= hunt_path %>">
  <header>
    <pre class="banner" aria-hidden="true">
 .--.         .--.
( (  )  )))  ( (  )   find me by ear
 '--'   )))   '--'
    </pre>
    <p>Give this page your microphone and nothing else. We'll try to find out where you are from the planes
      flying over you, even the ones you can't hear.</p>
  </header>

  <section data-hunt-target="intro">
    <h2>how</h2>
    <p>A propeller plane hums, and a jet's fan whines. As it passes you, that tone slides down in pitch (the
      Doppler effect), and the shape of that slide gives away its speed, how close it came, and the second it was closest. Every plane broadcasts
      where it is (ADS-B), so we look for the place on the ground where a real flight, right now, would have
      sounded exactly like what your microphone picked up. Two planes on different paths pin it down.</p>
    <p>Most of the time no plane comes close enough. Then all we have is your network's rough location and the
      hum of your mains power (50 Hz or 60 Hz), and you win.</p>

    <h2>what we keep</h2>
    <p>Your audio goes to our solver in 5 second pieces, stays in its memory while you listen, and is gone 30
      seconds after you stop. At the end you can drop a pin where you really are. We keep only how far off we
      were, and how far off your IP address alone was. No audio, no coordinates, no IP address, no account.</p>

    <div class="controls">
      <button type="button" data-hunt-target="start" data-action="hunt#start">find me</button>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">We listen until you press stop, or stop early once we're sure. The longer you leave
      it, the better the odds that a plane passes.
      <a href="<%= results_path %>">How often do we win?</a></p>
  </section>

  <p class="error" data-hunt-target="error" hidden></p>

  <section class="live" data-hunt-target="live" hidden>
    <p class="status"><span data-hunt-target="status"></span> <span class="muted" data-hunt-target="clock"></span></p>
    <div class="panels">
      <figure class="spectrogram">
        <canvas data-hunt-target="spectrogram"></canvas>
        <canvas class="overlay" data-hunt-target="overlay"></canvas>
        <figcaption class="muted small">your microphone, 40&ndash;8000 Hz (propellers low, jets high), whitened so faint tones show.
          Dashed: the curve a plane we matched should have made.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="map" data-hunt-target="map"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="controls">
      <button type="button" data-hunt-target="stop" data-action="hunt#stop">stop and guess</button>
      <button type="button" data-hunt-target="testFlight" data-action="hunt#testFlight" data-hunt-kind-param="prop" hidden>play a test flight</button>
      <button type="button" data-hunt-target="testFlight" data-action="hunt#testFlight" data-hunt-kind-param="jet" hidden>play a test jet</button>
    </div>
    <pre data-hunt-target="aircraft"></pre>
    <pre class="muted small" data-hunt-target="mic"></pre>

    <section class="reveal" data-hunt-target="reveal" hidden>
      <h2>our guess</h2>
      <p data-hunt-target="verdict"></p>
      <div data-hunt-target="pinPrompt">
        <p>Where are you really? Click the map, then send it. We'll store only the two distances.</p>
        <div class="controls">
          <button type="button" data-hunt-target="submitPin" data-action="hunt#submitPin" disabled>that's me</button>
          <button type="button" data-action="hunt#skip">I'd rather not say</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div data-hunt-target="score" hidden>
        <pre></pre>
        <p><a href="<%= root_path %>">try again</a> · <a href="<%= results_path %>">everyone's results</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>

  <footer>
    Method by <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UytYrhYLOKI">colsto</a>; solver forked from
    <a href="https://github.com/Bodila51/colsto-leak-and-mask">colsto-leak-and-mask</a>. Flight data taken from
    <a href="https://www.adsb.lol/">adsb.lol</a> (ODbL), elevation model is Copernicus DEM GLO-90, map &copy; OpenStreetMap
    , <a href="https://db-ip.com">IP Geolocation by DB-IP</a>.
  </footer>
</main>
